# Autonomous builds on Azure

Canonical content: `.cursor/skills/azure-autonomous-build/SKILL.md` and its `reference/` tree.
**Read `SKILL.md` before starting a sprint.** Do not fork the content into this file — two copies
of the same rules drifting apart is a failure this skill exists to prevent.

Set `alwaysApply: true` above if you want this loaded on every request.

## The ten that matter most

1. **Every sprint has ONE falsifiable Sprint Goal, written as an exit test.** "Payments are
   implemented" cannot fail; "a replayed webhook produces exactly one transition and one payment
   row" can. The loop ends when that goal is green on a squash-merged PR.

2. **ONE slice owns the integration point** — the route, the mount, the wiring — runs LAST against
   merged main, and its exit test walks the real journey with no hand-constructed URL. Features
   have shipped complete, CI-green and unreachable four times. Assume a fifth.

3. **Gates fan out**: N verifiers over disjoint areas, then one synthesiser. Verifiers find; they
   do not fix. **The synthesiser must downgrade any claimed PASS whose evidence could not have
   failed** — a dev-mode check for a production-only defect, a test asserting the absence of an
   error string, a permission check run as the database owner.

4. **A missing agent report is UNVERIFIED, never a pass.** Silence must not read as success.

5. **Reproduce on a production build.** Dev mode hid a CSP defect that broke every client-side
   navigation in the app.

6. **Verify state, never output.** A pipeline's exit status is the LAST command's, so
   `deploy.sh … | tail` reports 0 on a failed deploy. Query the control plane, the database, the
   endpoint.

7. **Every route registers in the release/feature gate**, or it is a 404 indistinguishable from a
   route that was never written. **Every DB write needs a COLUMN-SCOPED grant** — a table-level
   check passes while the columns actually written are ungranted.

8. **Deploy only through the wrapper script, always with the image parameter.** A raw cloud-CLI
   deployment silently skips gated app resources and reports success. Deploy once per phase,
   before each gate, never into an in-flight CI run.

9. **Uploads:** provider-native malware scanning proven with a real EICAR file; content sniffing
   never extension; short-lived permission-checked signed URLs with attachment disposition from a
   private per-record namespace; managed identity, never account keys.

10. **Never rename the required aggregating CI check** — it blocks every PR in the repository. And
    don't merge while parallel agents hold open PRs: with up-to-date-branch protection, every
    merge puts the others behind at the cost of a rebase and a full CI pass.

When something breaks, check `reference/failure-signatures.md` before diagnosing from scratch.
